WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.357 line:85%
Shhh... I'm listening to the Moon!

2
00:00:03.447 --> 00:00:07.806 line:85%
We're the Apollo seismometers, super-sensitive listeners.

3
00:00:07.896 --> 00:00:15.022 line:85%
Astronauts set us up at their landing sites, starting with Apollo 11 in 1969.

4
00:00:15.112 --> 00:00:18.543 line:85%
Every day, we felt for tiny shakes in the ground.

5
00:00:18.633 --> 00:00:20.949 line:85%
And we found them: moonquakes!

6
00:00:21.039 --> 00:00:24.094 line:85%
We even recorded the first artificial moonquake.

7
00:00:24.184 --> 00:00:33.161 line:85%
The stations from Apollo 12, 14, 15 and 16 kept listening until September 30, 1977.

8
00:00:33.251 --> 00:00:38.174 line:85%
Our recordings helped scientists study the Moon's crust and interior.

9
00:00:38.264 --> 00:00:41.048 line:85%
What do you think makes the Moon shake?
